Habitat Ring
   The two Habitat Rings are each approximately 10m wide, with an outer diameter of 140m, and comprised of three decks. Each of these decks have simulated gravity from centrifugal force, and are connected to the main hull of the Odyssey through four turbo-lifts. The three decks are designated Decks 1-3 with the outermost deck being Deck 1 and the innermost deck being Deck 3. The ring rotates at a constant speed of 3.3 rpm's which offer around 80% of earths gravity without any negative effects to most humans.
   Deck 1 is designated as 'The Promenade', and is composed of four Cafe Courtyards centered on the four turbo-lifts with 94m long hallways linking the courtyards full of rooms dedicated to dining, recreation, fitness, and medical services.
   Deck 2 is home to Officers Quarters, VIP passengers, and rooms for synthetic companions. It has four Cafe Courtyards centered on the four turbo-lifts with 36m long hallways that open into lounges before continuing down another 36m hallway to link to the next Cafe Courtyard. Within each 36m section of hallway are the personal rooms of varying sizes and communal public bathrooms. When at full capacity this ring can comfortably house 70 crew & passengers.
   Deck 3 is home to regular crew and passengers. It has four Cafe Courtyards centered on the four turbo-lifts with 33m long hallways that open into lounges before continuing down another 33m hallway to link to the next Cafe Courtyard. Within each 33m section of hallway are many rooms of varying sizes, plus multiple communal public bathrooms. When at full capacity this ring can comfortably house 130 crew & passengers.

