Turbo-lifts
   Four massive spokes connect the habitat rings to the main body of the UNSS Odyssey, through which a single turbo-lift shaft passes in each. Due to the spokes constantly rotating around a central core the four turbo-lifts stop within the zero-g section of the inner hull and then moves within a lateral tunnel to match speeds with the rotating spokes and then moves vertically to get up to the habitat rings. With am interior size of 2.5m x 2.5m, each turbo-lift has a total area of 6.25 sq meters, which can comfortably fit around 20 but has a maximum occupancy of 35. Each turbo-lift can go to each individual deck and each individual Cafe Courtyard within each deck.

Deck 1, Promenade
   The Promenade is split into four quarters, each of which is centered on one of the four Cafe Courtyards. A 2.5m wide hallway travels along the outer wall of the deck with the side of the hallway alternating between cafe courtyards. The entire deck has been designed in such a way as to give the illusion of moving through an open air pedestrian oriented commercial area with individual rooms designed to look like separate buildings.
   The Social Quarter is centered on a Mediterranean themed cafe courtyard, with a small Mexican restaurant named Salsa Inferno on the spin-ward side of the courtyard, and an Italian restaurant named La Dolce Vita on the other. Moving away from the courtyard spin-ward is the Amber Lounge, Pulse, and Quarks before moving into Wellness Quarter. Moving the other direction is Lumina, the Holly Theatre, and the Vortex Music Room before moving into the Americana Quarter.
   The Wellness Quarter is centered on tropical garden themed cafe courtyard, with a Juice Bar caked Nature’s Nectar spin-ward, followed by ZenFlex Fitness, and then Dwayne's Gymnasium before moving into the Social Quarter. Moving the other direction is a restaurant named The Mindful Meal, followed by the Odyssey Medical Center, Modern Warfare, and a number of small micro-climate rooms before moving into the Civic Quarter.
   The Civic Quarter centered on a ultra-modern urban themed cafe courtyard with The Pancake House on the spin-ward side, and Big Al's on the other side. Moving down the hall from The Pancake House is Kaylin's Laundry Services, Mai's Vietnamese Barbershop, and The Zen Den before moving into the Wellness Quarter. Moving the other direction behind Big Al's is The Maker’s Node, Petopia, Deana's Interior Designs, and The Fun Room before moving into the Americana Quarter.
   The Americana Quarter is centered on a small town USA themed Cafe Courtyard with an Asian Fusion Restaurant named Jade & Bamboo on the spin-ward side, and Pit Boss BBQ on the other. In the hallway leading past Jade & Bamboo is Nina's Art Studio, the Odyssey Library & Museum, Artistic Designs, Timberlake's Game Room, and Kinky Needs before moving into the Civic Quarter. On the other side past Pit Boss BBQ is Backblast Arms & Armor, KZ Clothiers, Expeditions Unlimited, and the Odyssey Religious Center before moving into the Social Quarter.

