Deck 2, Officers Quarters
   Deck 2 of the habitat ring features the same cafe courtyard with turbo-lift access as Deck 1, but instead of creating the illusion of an outdoor setting, these small courtyards look more like the lobby of a high-end hotel. While each of the four areas is styled differently, they share certain design elements such as a food fabrication station, comfortable seating, artwork on the walls, and rich colors. Between each of these courtyards is a long 2m wide hallway with doors to the rooms of the individual rooms & public bathrooms until reaching an open lounge style sitting area midway between courtyards. These open lounge style areas are communal spaces where people can socialize, play games, or even relax a bit like a large public living room. All of the individual rooms on this deck have a single bed and are designed for either an individual or a couple, and can be compared to a 3-4 star hotel in style and amenities. Deck 2 is where the entire normal operations crew of the UNSS Odyssey lives, as do the Synthetic Humanoid Companions. Up to 70 people plus 30 synthetics can live comfortably on this deck.

Deck 3, Crew Quarters
   Deck 3 of the habitat ring features the same indoor courtyard with turbo-lift access as Deck 2, but instead of looking like the lobby of a high-end hotel, these courtyards look more like those of an office building or mall. While these courtyards are almost identical in overall layout to those on Deck 2, the overall quality of furnishings & artwork are lower, being designed for much more durability than those on deck 2. In between sections of 2m wide hallway, deck 3 also features open style lounge areas, but with simpler & more durable design than those of deck 2. Most of the rooms on this deck have either 2 individual beds or a pair of bunk beds, and can be compared to a 2-3 star hotel in style and amenities. Up to 180 people can live comfortably on this deck.

Cafe Courtyards
   Each Cafe Courtyard measures approximately 10m x 15m with a large central turbo-lift enclosure in the center. On levels 2 & 3 the turbo-lift enclosure has food fabricator stations built into the left & right flanks. Filling a large portion of the room, with the exception of walking paths and the turbo-lift enclosure, are a large number of comfortable 2 person tables, with total seating for around 30-40 people at a single time. On deck 1 the Cafe Courtyard is flanked on either side with small restaurants with additional seating for multiple people, but on decks 2 & 3 the courtyard is flanked by interior walls that divide the courtyard interior from the hallway leading to individual rooms. Within each cafe courtyard on decks 2 & 3 these interior walls are what really help define that courtyard, with one courtyard having an indoor wall fountain and another a wall of ivy.

Lounge Sitting Areas
   Each Lounge Sitting Area measures approximately 10m x 15m and features a large number of comfortable sitting areas, a game table, a large screen Trid TV, and a centrally located holo-table with a game station for playing multi-player competitive holo-games like 'Mech Battle 4' or 'Deadly Arena 6'. There is enough seating for up to around 80 people to sit casually or around 110 people sitting close together.

Rooms
   On Deck 2 all rooms have individual bathrooms and available space for personalization. These rooms are also coated with smart materials which allow the texture and color of almost everything within the room to be customized by the occupant. This can be done via computer terminal, AR glasses, or cybernetic implants and allows the occupant to choose from among many overall aesthetic styles or on a piece-by-piece basis.
   On Deck 3 the rooms are also coated with smart materials which allow the texture and color of almost everything within the room to be customized, but the customization can only be done by an authorized interior designer with the express permission of all occupants, and only from among pre-programmed aesthetic styles.

